e - probably not an index): audio_encoder.encoder.layers.{i}.lstm.bias_hh_l1 hole 0 == 13 DEGENERATE hole (one value - probably not an index): audio_encoder.encoder.layers.{i}.lstm.bias_ih_l0 hole 0 == 13 DEGENERATE hole (one value - probably not an index): audio_encoder.encoder.layers.{i}.lstm.bias_ih_l1 hole 0 == 13 DEGENERATE hole (one value - probably not an index): audio_encoder.encoder.layers.{i}.lstm.weight_hh_l0 hole 0 == 13 DEGENERATE hole (one value - probably not an index): audio_encoder.encoder.layers.{i}.lstm.weight_hh_l1 hole 0 == 13 DEGENERATE hole (one value - probably not an index): audio_encoder.encoder.layers.{i}.lstm.weight_ih_l0 hole 0 == 13 DEGENERATE hole (one value - probably not an index): audio_encoder.encoder.layers.{i}.lstm.weight_ih_l1 hole 0 == 13. RATIFICATION OWED: (1) The repo also ships a state_dict.bin / compression_state_dict.bin pair (the audiocraft\npackaging) and an fp32 index. Only the safetensors packaging is described. (2) ROLES are mechanical (role == pattern). Rename any tensor whose bytes are the same bytes another packaging spells differently - that is the only thing that makes a cross-packaging derive possible instead of a refusal. (3) FUSIONS are undeclared. A header cannot see a fused axis, so a fused qkv/gate-up must be declared by a human reading the model's config (head count, hidden size); a wrong one is a ~90%-error split that never crashes. (4) SETS are undeclared (no subset-snapshot groups). (5) COMPONENT SCOPE is the caller's: declaring a shared encoder ties this document to every family that ships the same one (tensorfs#121).",
